Instruction: Read the following segments of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the timing requirement for representations and warranties.\nQuestion: When are the representations and warranties required to be valid according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: At Closing Only\nOption B: At Signing & At Closing\n\nMerger Agreement Segment One: Section 10.4 Conditions Precedent to the Merger. The Company’s representations and warranties set forth in Article IV of this Agreement must be true and correct as of the date of execution and must continue to be true and correct at the Closing Date. This dual timing requirement applies uniformly without allowances for materiality exceptions unless expressly modified herein. (Page 92)\n\nMerger Agreement Segment Two: Section 14.2 Representations and Warranties Adjustments. Notwithstanding Section 10.4, in the event that any factual discrepancies are identified after execution, the representations and warranties shall be reassessed solely on the basis of their status at Closing. (Page 104)
