Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the timing of the required representations and warranties.\nQuestion: According to the bring down provision, when must the representations and warranties be valid?\nOption A: At Closing Only\nOption B: At Signing & At Closing\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 8.4 Conditions Precedent to Closing. Subject to limited de minimis exceptions, all representations and warranties of the Company shall be true and correct as of the execution date of this Agreement, and they must be reconfirmed as true and correct as of the Closing Date as if made on and as of that date. (Page 112)\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 9.1 Representations and Warranties. Except as expressly modified, the representations and warranties stated herein shall remain in full force and effect at the time of Signing and must be revalidated to reflect their truth and accuracy as of the Closing Date, thereby requiring dual confirmation.
