Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the timing requirement for representations and warranties. Question: Under the bring down mechanism of the Agreement, when must the Company's representations and warranties be confirmed? Option A: Only at Closing. Option B: At Signing and again at Closing.

Merger Agreement Excerpt: Section 9.1 Timing of Representations. Except for those representations expressly qualified as effective solely as of the Signing Date per Section 9.1(a), every representation and warranty provided by the Company shall be true as of the Signing Date and must be reconfirmed as of the Closing Date pursuant to the bring down procedure set forth in Section 9.1(b). Where a representation is limited by an explicit 'as-of' signing qualification, no further confirmation at Closing is required; however, in the absence of such qualification, the default requirement is a dual confirmation at both Signing and Closing. Notwithstanding any other provision in this Agreement, the bring down verification shall serve to ensure that all non-qualified representations are accurate at two distinct temporal milestones.
Choices:
